diff --git a/docs/kaede-av1-e2ee.md b/docs/kaede-av1-e2ee.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..63a7aea
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/kaede-av1-e2ee.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Kaede AV1 E2EE build
+
+This branch applies the same authenticated AV1 framing used by Kaede's patched
+Rust and browser SDKs to the m137 native dependency used by Flutter WebRTC 1.2.1.
+The source revision is pinned in VERSION and the workflow. Builds produce an
+Android AAR and an Apple XCFramework as CI artifacts; they do not publish releases.
+
+The crypto patch preserves canonical AV1 OBU headers, sequence configuration and
+frame-type bits, authenticates those clear bytes with AES-GCM, and puts the IV,
+tag and key index into a final, versioned metadata OBU. Malformed lengths and
+missing tags are rejected before indexing. AV1 framing is a Kaede extension,
+not compatible with unpatched LiveKit AV1 encryption. Other codecs are unchanged.
+
+Use both artifacts together with the matching browser/Rust SDK patches. Do not
+activate encrypted AV1 in Flutter against the old hosted native binaries.
+Physical-device testing remains required after building and integrating them.
